crates/workspace-tools/sandbox/README.md:108:With `container.modelProxy.enable`, both send their requests to a model proxy on the host instead, and no account sign-in enters the container. The proxy is [Coda's ungate](https://github.com/Coda-Health/ungate): it keeps the Claude and ChatGPT sign-ins as an account pool, passes Claude Code's `/v1/messages` and Codex's `/v1/responses` through to them, and records usage per client key. Run it on the host listening on `hostAddress` as well as loopback (its `HOST` takes a comma-separated list, and it binds `hostAddress` once the container's interface exists), on `container.modelProxy.port`, 47821 by default. Mint a client key for the container in its dashboard, then store it:
